            Paragraph(Text("The head is the literal signed integer set {-n,0,n}. At each exterior magnitude, the two coordinates are the actual positive and negative arithmetic coupling columns. Their square-summable sequence is an element of a complex Hilbert direct sum at every natural cutoff.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The source map is complex linear. Its Gram quadratic form equals the complete infinite sum of the paired column energy, for arbitrary complex coefficients including zero and cancellation.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The even, odd and second-difference heads have respective normalization factors 1/sqrt(3), 1/sqrt(2) and 1/sqrt(6). For n!=0 their node Gram is the identity, so the sum of squared original retained coefficients equals the Euclidean coefficient mass.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Finite-head zero-energy reconstruction and this original metric imply positive definiteness of the actual three-column Gram at every cutoff. For exterior cutoffs the sharp two-sign denominator comparison also controls the finite physical energy.")),
